  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Troeven. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Troeven is a Dutch/Flemish trick-taking game where players start at a score (e.g., 7) and work down to zero. Uses a 32-card deck (7-A). The trump caller picks trump from first 4-5 cards. Win more card-value points (A=4, K=3, Q=2, J=1) than opponents to reduce score by 1. If trump caller loses, their team gains a point (penalty).',
    objective: 'Be the first team to cancel all seven branches (reduce your score from 7 to 0) by winning more card points than the opponents in each hand; the team that called trumps and loses adds a branch.',
    gameplay: 'Trump caller declares trump. Play 8 tricks. Follow suit. Total 40 card points. Higher scorer reduces score by 1. Tie = no change. Trump caller losing = adds 1 (penalty).',
